   PRE-INSTALLATION

   netMHCpan 4.2 currently runs under Darwin (macOS), and Linux.
   The package consists of two files:
  
      netMHCpan-4.2.readme         this file
      netMHCpan-4.2.<unix>.tar.gz   compressed TAR archive

   where 'unix' is the UNIX platform on which you are about to install. After
   installation the software will occupy less than 45 MB of diskspace.

   INSTALLATION

   1. Uncompress and untar the package:

      cat netMHCpan-4.2.<unix>.tar.gz | tar -xzvf -

      This will produce a directory 'netMHCpan-4.2'.

   2. In the 'netMHCpan-4.2' directory edit the script 'netMHCpan':
   
      a. At the top of the file  locate the part labelled  "GENERAL SETTINGS:
         CUSTOMIZE TO YOUR SITE"  and set  the 'NMHOME' variable  to the full
	     path to the 'netMHCpan-4.2' directory on your system;

      b. Set TMPDIR to the full path to the temporary directory of you choice. It must
         be user-writable. You may for example set it to $NMHOME/tmp (and create
         the tmp folder in the netMHCpan-4.2 directory).

   3. In the 'netMHCpan-4.2/test' directory test the software:

      >../netMHCpan -p test.pep > test.pep.out
      >../netMHCpan -p -context test.pep_context > test.pep_context.out
      >../netMHCpan -pmhc test.pep_mhc > test.pep_mhc.out
      >../netMHCpan -pmhc -context test.pep_context_mhc > test.pep_context_mhc.out
      >../netMHCpan -p test.pep -BA > test.pep_wBA.out
      >../netMHCpan test.fsa > test.fsa.out
      >../netMHCpan -hlaseq B0702.fsa -p test.pep > test.pep_userMHC.out
      >../netMHCpan -p test.pep -BA -xls -a HLA-A01:01,HLA-A02:01 -xlsfile NetMHCpan_out.xls

      The resulting ".myout" files should not differ from the corresponding
      ".out" files provided in the package other than in the directory names
	  and small rounding errors.

   4. Finish the installation:

      a. Copy or link the 'netMHCpan' file to a directory in the users' path.

      b. Copy the 'netMHCpan.1' file to a location  in your manual system. If
         you need a compiled version try running:

         man -d netMHCpan.1 | compress >netMHCpan.Z

         or:

         neqn netMHCpan.1 | tbl | nroff -man | col | compress >netMHCpan.Z

   5. Enjoy ...


